<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Vertières</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1803">1803</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haitian-revolution">Haitian Revolution</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Vertières was fought on 18 November 1803 outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cap-haitien">Cap-Français</a>, when the Haitian revolutionary army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-jacques-dessalines">Jean-Jacques Dessalines</a>, with François Capois prominent in the assault, defeated the French forces of General Rochambeau. It was the last major battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haitian-revolution">Haitian Revolution</a>: Rochambeau agreed to evacuate the colony, and Dessalines proclaimed the independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> on 1 January 1804.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-vertieres.jpg" alt="Battle of Vertières" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kitanago · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vertieres.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
